ReactionFlow is a new project intended to extract and generalize reaction-event and reaction-path
automation that was initially developed in the private MatEnsemble repository.

Extraction baseline:

    Repository: Austin243/MatEnsemble-private
    Commit: c1b212296a0b6a3b7dec3a927e81cb7bd6d0125e
    License: BSD 3-Clause

`src/reactionflow/detection.py` adapts the geometric detector from
`src/matensemble/analysis/bonds.py` at the baseline commit. Its identity contract and public API
have been generalized for ReactionFlow. `src/reactionflow/candidates.py` adapts generic tracking
and exact graph identity from `src/matensemble/reactions/core.py`; its element-specific handoff
policy was not copied. `src/reactionflow/store.py` adapts the occurrence registry and atomic
candidate publication from those baseline sources without MatEnsemble controller coupling.
Detailed extraction notes are maintained in `docs/provenance.md`.

As further implementation is moved or adapted, the MatEnsemble copyright and license notice must
remain preserved and the provenance ledger must be updated.
